node 451 · 451 · ⟦FAHRENHEIT 451:451:f1daf3⟧

WHO   — FAHRENHEIT 451 — a NOUTHESIA book-world
WHAT  — Ray Bradbury · 1953 · the temperature at which books burn
WHERE — Fahrenheit 451 (Ray Bradbury, 1953)  Framework inputs: Fahrenheit 451 (Ray Bradbury, 1953)  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — No tyrant had to ban the books — we put them down for the wall-screens first; the resistance is just this: read, be still, and become someone who remembers.
HOW   — Guy Montag, a fireman who burns books for a living, is jolted awake by his curious neighbour Clarisse and by a woman who chooses to burn alive with her library. He begins stealing books, finds a guide in the old professor Faber, and is hunted by his fire chief Beatty and the Mechanical Hound — until, with the city's screens blaring, war erupts, the city is bombed, and Montag escapes downriver to the Book People, exiles who have each memorised a book to keep it alive.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
